# Bilingual meeting-summary format

Produce the **full report in English, then the full report in 繁體中文**, at
*identical structure and equal detail*. Every section, bullet, and table row that
appears in one language appears in the other. English first, then a divider, then
Chinese. Render everything as Markdown.

## Processing rules (what makes it useful)
- **Read the whole transcript first.** Identify attendees, topic, date.
- **Tag substance, drop filler.** Keep questions, data points/metrics, discussion
  points, decisions, and action items. Cut greetings, scheduling chatter, "嗯/啊/
  就是說/那個" and English filler.
- **Stay neutral on identity.** Refer to people by name or by what they did (the
  host, the presenter, a participant, the other party). Never label anyone a
  "customer"/"client" or frame it "us vs. them" unless the transcript explicitly
  says so. This works for internal syncs, trainings, partner, and client calls
  alike — let the reader infer roles.
- **Preserve specifics exactly.** Names, figures, %, amounts, dates, deadlines,
  and technical terms stay verbatim. If a number wasn't stated, don't supply one.
- **Mark uncertainty, don't smooth it.** Flag ambiguous or likely mis-heard
  content with `[待確認]` / `[to confirm]`. If you fix an obvious transcription
  error from context, mark it `[*]`.
- **Owner column stays blank** in the To-Do table — the user fills it in.
- **Quote sparingly** — only a short, load-bearing line.
- **Never fabricate or extend.** Organize only what's in the input.

## Section order (use in BOTH languages, identical)
1. **Basic Information / 基本資訊** — Date / 日期, Attendees / 與會人員, Topic / 主題
   (and meeting type / 會議性質 only if obvious). Use "待補 / TBD" for anything
   not stated.
2. **Summary / 摘要** — 3–5 sentences on purpose, main progress, and conclusion.
3. **Q&A Recap / 問答彙整** — questions raised and the responses given. Attribute
   neutrally. Mark open items (e.g. "To confirm / 待確認").
4. **Key Data & Metrics / 關鍵數據與指標** — every concrete number (amounts, %,
   dates, performance figures, market size). Keep exact; never invent.
5. **Discussion Points / 討論重點** — organized by theme, each with a sub-heading.
   Convert speech to concise written prose.
6. **Decisions / 決議事項** — consensus reached, policy changes, final calls.
7. **To-Do & Ownership / 待辦事項與分工** — our action items (table below).
8. **Commitments from Others / 對方承諾事項** — things people outside our own team
   said they'd do/deliver for us. Attribute by name/role, neutrally. Include form
   and timing/status. Omit the section only if no such commitment was made.
9. **Next Meeting / 下次會議規劃** — time, expected topics, attendees — only if
   mentioned; otherwise "未提及 / Not mentioned."

## To-Do & Ownership table (Owner column blank)

English:
```
| Topic / Detail | Action | Format | Owner |
|----------------|--------|--------|-------|
| [topic + the key point raised] | [the action] | [doc / slides / email / data sample…] | |
```
繁體中文:
```
| 主題／內容 | 你要做的事 | 形式 | 負責 |
|-----------|-----------|------|------|
| [主題＋當下提出的重點] | [對應要做的事] | [文件／簡報／Email／數據樣本…] | |
```
One-line note under each table:
*Owner left blank for manual input (Team A / Team B / Both). / 負責欄留空，請自行填入（Team A／Team B／兩者）。*

## Commitments from Others table

English:
```
| Deliverable / Commitment | Promised by | Form | Expected timing / status |
|--------------------------|-------------|------|--------------------------|
| [what they said they'd provide/do] | [name or role] | [doc / data / intro / email…] | [date, "TBD," or status] |
```
繁體中文:
```
| 承諾事項／交付 | 承諾者 | 形式 | 預計時間／狀態 |
|---------------|--------|------|----------------|
| [對方表示會提供或處理的事項] | [姓名或角色] | [文件／資料／引薦／Email…] | [日期、「待補」或狀態] |
```

## Language divider
Between the English and Chinese halves, emit a clear divider so the switch is
obvious in the rendered doc, e.g. a line of `---` (a horizontal rule) followed by
the Chinese H1 title. Keep the two halves in one `markdown_text` payload.
